WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.617
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A one.

2
00:00:05.917 --> 00:00:09.234
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.534 --> 00:00:14.891
Unit thirty-five: Adverbs of Manner. Today you will describe how things are done.

4
00:00:15.191 --> 00:00:17.797
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.733 --> 00:00:21.897
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:23.647
Quickly.

7
00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:26.580
Quickly means in a fast way.

8
00:00:27.183 --> 00:00:28.393
She runs quickly.

9
00:00:28.983 --> 00:00:31.694
Your turn. Say: Quickly.

10
00:00:34.533 --> 00:00:35.523
Quickly.

11
00:00:36.283 --> 00:00:37.250
Slowly.

12
00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:40.087
Slowly means in a slow way.

13
00:00:40.683 --> 00:00:42.311
The turtle moves slowly.

14
00:00:42.917 --> 00:00:45.197
Your turn. Say: Slowly.

15
00:00:48.033 --> 00:00:48.988
Slowly.

16
00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:50.705
Carefully.

17
00:00:51.717 --> 00:00:53.670
Carefully means in a careful way.

18
00:00:54.283 --> 00:00:55.795
Carry the glass carefully.

19
00:00:56.383 --> 00:00:59.210
Your turn. Say: Carefully.

20
00:01:02.067 --> 00:01:03.021
Carefully.

21
00:01:03.783 --> 00:01:04.459
Well.

22
00:01:05.450 --> 00:01:06.869
Well means in a good way.

23
00:01:07.483 --> 00:01:09.088
He speaks English well.

24
00:01:09.683 --> 00:01:11.941
Your turn. Say: Well.

25
00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:15.580
Well.

26
00:01:16.317 --> 00:01:17.202
Badly.

27
00:01:18.217 --> 00:01:19.856
Badly means in a bad way.

28
00:01:20.450 --> 00:01:21.753
I slept badly.

29
00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:24.782
Your turn. Say: Badly.

30
00:01:27.633 --> 00:01:28.518
Badly.

31
00:01:29.283 --> 00:01:30.250
Loudly.

32
00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:33.064
Loudly means in a loud way.

33
00:01:33.650 --> 00:01:35.057
They shouted loudly.

34
00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:38.070
Your turn. Say: Loudly.

35
00:01:40.933 --> 00:01:41.958
Loudly.

36
00:01:42.717 --> 00:01:43.544
Quietly.

37
00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:46.283
Quietly means in a quiet way.

38
00:01:46.883 --> 00:01:48.755
Speak quietly in the library.

39
00:01:49.350 --> 00:01:51.619
Your turn. Say: Quietly.

40
00:01:54.467 --> 00:01:55.456
Quietly.

41
00:01:56.217 --> 00:01:57.032
Manner.

42
00:01:58.017 --> 00:02:00.365
Manner means the way in which something is done.

43
00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:02.903
Adverbs of manner tell how.

44
00:02:03.517 --> 00:02:05.612
Your turn. Say: Manner.

45
00:02:08.467 --> 00:02:09.363
Manner.

46
00:02:10.167 --> 00:02:13.922
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:14.783 --> 00:02:18.550
Visal, how do you walk to school? Quickly or slowly?

48
00:02:19.650 --> 00:02:27.135
I walk quickly because I am often late. Quickly is an adverb of manner. It tells us how someone does something.

49
00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:29.774
How do we make adverbs?

50
00:02:30.883 --> 00:02:43.683
Add -ly to an adjective: slow, slowly; careful, carefully; quiet, quietly. If the adjective ends in y, change it to i: happy, happily.

51
00:02:44.783 --> 00:02:46.957
Are there any irregular adverbs?

52
00:02:48.050 --> 00:03:00.439
Yes! Good becomes well: She sings well. Fast and hard keep the same form: He runs fast. She works hard. Adverbs usually come after the verb or the object.

53
00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:03.019
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:03.883 --> 00:03:07.717
Grammar focus: Adverbs of manner: verb plus adverb.

55
00:03:08.017 --> 00:03:09.285
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:09.983 --> 00:03:11.286
She runs quickly.

57
00:03:12.183 --> 00:03:13.846
He speaks English well.

58
00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:16.355
Please speak quietly.

59
00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:25.981
Add -ly to an adjective to make an adverb of manner. Good becomes well; fast and hard stay the same. The adverb usually comes after the verb.

60
00:03:26.717 --> 00:03:30.379
Be careful! Don't say: He drives careful.

61
00:03:32.333 --> 00:03:34.275
Say: He drives carefully.

62
00:03:34.575 --> 00:03:36.853
Use the adverb carefully after a verb.

63
00:03:37.667 --> 00:03:40.156
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:40.967 --> 00:03:42.095
How Do You Do It?.

65
00:03:42.395 --> 00:03:45.568
My sister runs quickly, but my brother walks slowly.

66
00:03:46.567 --> 00:03:48.659
Please carry the glass carefully.

67
00:03:49.667 --> 00:03:52.549
He speaks English well, and she sings beautifully.

68
00:03:53.533 --> 00:03:55.591
In the library, we speak quietly.

69
00:03:56.600 --> 00:03:58.797
At the stadium, people shout loudly.

70
00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:03.786
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:06.722
She sings blank. (good)

72
00:04:07.022 --> 00:04:09.909
A, good. B, well. C, goodly.

73
00:04:13.467 --> 00:04:15.025
The answer is B: well.

74
00:04:16.183 --> 00:04:18.334
He walks blank because he is tired.

75
00:04:18.634 --> 00:04:22.067
A, slow. B, slowly. C, slowy.

76
00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:27.600
The answer is B: slowly.

77
00:04:28.750 --> 00:04:30.761
Please speak blank in the library.

78
00:04:31.061 --> 00:04:34.448
A, quietly. B, quiet. C, loud.

79
00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:39.849
The answer is A: quietly.

80
00:04:40.983 --> 00:04:42.936
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:43.236 --> 00:04:48.980
A, He drives carefully.. B, He drives careful.. C, He carefully drives a car in..

82
00:04:52.533 --> 00:04:55.404
The answer is A: He drives carefully..

83
00:04:56.550 --> 00:04:59.130
According to the reading, who walks slowly?

84
00:04:59.430 --> 00:05:03.745
A, my brother. B, my sister. C, my mother.

85
00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:09.369
The answer is A: my brother.

86
00:05:10.567 --> 00:05:13.614
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:14.450 --> 00:05:17.053
Write one sentence about how you walk or speak.

88
00:05:25.850 --> 00:05:27.362
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:27.662 --> 00:05:40.534
I walk quickly to school because the road is short, and I speak quietly in the library. I use quickly and quietly because they are adverbs of manner. They tell my teacher how I do things.

90
00:05:40.834 --> 00:05:42.566
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:43.450 --> 00:05:48.854
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and adverbs of manner: verb plus adverb.

92
00:05:49.154 --> 00:05:53.687
Today's value is self-awareness. Know your strengths and keep growing.

93
00:05:53.987 --> 00:05:57.023
See you in Unit thirty-six. Goodbye!

94
00:05:57.323 --> 00:06:00.439
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

